Title: "The Real Numbers"
Id: "d18bf879-7408-48c4-b09f-60d5fb20b183"


Text: "The real number system $\mathbb{R}$ extends the rational numbers to form
       a complete continuum. It is uniquely characterized up to isomorphism as a
       complete ordered field, ensuring that every bounded set of reals
       possesses a least upper bound (supremum)."
Id: "2f7605c2-086a-4429-a969-dd003a83531e"


SectionTitle: "The Real Field"
Id: "0d082d38-e717-4330-b29d-e67f0717341c"


[\reals]
Defines: Rb ::= (R, 0, 1, +, *, -, /, <=, neg(x_))
abstractly:
specifies:
. R is \set
. 0 "in" R
. 1 "in" R
. + is \binary.operation:on{R}
. * is \binary.operation:on{R}
. - is \binary.operation:on{R}
. / is \binary.operation:on{R}
. <= is \total.order:on{R}
. neg is \function:on{R}:to{R}
expresses:
. 0 != 1
. forAll: a, b, c "in" R
  then:
  . (a + b) + c = a + (b + c)
  . a + b = b + a
  . a + 0 = a
  . (a * b) * c = a * (b * c)
  . a * b = b * a
  . a * 1 = a
  . a * (b + c) = (a * b) + (a * c)
Enables:
. capability: x_ "in" Rb :-> x_ is \real
. view:
  as: S := R is \set
Documented:
. called: "the reals"
. written: "\mathbb{R}"
. description: "The real numbers $(\mathbb{R}, 0, 1, +, \cdot, \le)$ as a
                complete ordered field."
Id: "aeec4453-1166-47cd-a5f4-3eed295b3d15"


[\real]
Declares: x "in" \reals..R
Enables:
. capability: a_ + b_ :=> a_ \.real.+./ b_
. capability: a_ - b_ :=> a_ \.real.-./ b_
. capability: a_ * b_ :=> a_ \.real.*./ b_
. capability: a_ / b_ :=> a_ \.real.div./ b_
. capability: -a_ :=> \real.neg(a_)
Documented:
. called: "real"
. description: "A real number is a member of the underlying carrier set
                $\mathbb{R}$."
Id: "cc52bbbc-d925-469e-9252-2fad913ba14b"


[\real.zero]
Defines: z := \reals..0 is \real
Documented:
. called: "real zero"
. written: "0"
Id: "945650d9-8dab-4716-b4f7-2714e2219af9"


[\real.one]
Defines: o := \reals..1 is \real
Documented:
. called: "real one"
. written: "1"
Id: "1965d580-9b4d-4d19-93ee-82ebb75d1834"


[a_ \.real.+./ b_]
Defines: a_ + b_ := \reals..`+`(a_, b_) is \real
Documented:
. called: "$a_?$ plus $b_?$"
. written: "a_? + b_?"
Id: "c6dc7fde-38f1-4e5b-a80a-2153567efe6f"


[a_ \.real.-./ b_]
Defines: a_ - b_ := \reals..`-`(a_, b_) is \real
Documented:
. called: "$a_?$ minus $b_?$"
. written: "a_? - b_?"
Id: "6daad43c-b638-4a51-b600-4c17a3d9a066"


[a_ \.real.*./ b_]
Defines: a_ * b_ := \reals..`*`(a_, b_) is \real
Documented:
. called: "$a_?$ times $b_?$"
. written: "a_? \cdot b_?"
Id: "cde6b01e-d8c3-4996-b69a-1fdca9e69385"


[a_ \.real.div./ b_]
Defines: a_ / b_ := \reals..`/`(a_, b_) is \real
Documented:
. called: "$a_?$ divided by $b_?$"
. written: "\frac{a_?}{b_?}"
Id: "33d587f9-8ec0-4f27-8c65-42daae86748a"


[\real.neg(a_)]
Defines: n := \reals..neg(a_) is \real
Documented:
. called: "negative of $a_?$"
. written: "-a_?"
Id: "9b876af6-034f-4fb7-bc5f-af41345891fb"


[a \:real.leq:/ b]
Declares: a is \real
when: b is \\anything
Documented:
. called: "$a?$ is less than or equal to $b?$"
. written: "a? \leq b?"
Id: "d6f542fa-34a7-4359-9b32-78bb28af098a"


[a \:real.less:/ b]
Declares: a is \real
when: b is \\anything
Documented:
. called: "$a?$ is less than $b?$"
. written: "a? < b?"
Id: "5b8f85c7-135a-4702-b5aa-1d61f526ae99"


[a \:real.geq:/ b]
Declares: a is \real
when: b is \\anything
Documented:
. called: "$a?$ is greater than or equal to $b?$"
. written: "a? \geq b?"
Id: "53068503-7473-4378-a2bd-d6aa98d1f9d5"


[a \:real.greater:/ b]
Declares: a is \real
when: b is \\anything
Documented:
. called: "$a?$ is greater than $b?$"
. written: "a? > b?"
Id: "b0fef5ae-f1c8-46ab-b057-4000e9fda5d1"


SectionTitle: "Absolute Value and Bounds"
Id: "231d1127-646d-4845-88b1-f0ee9114a0a4"


[\real.abs(x_)]
Defines: a is \real
expresses:
. piecewise:
  if: x_ \:real.geq?:/ \real.zero
  then: a = x_
  else: a = \real.neg(x_)
Documented:
. called: "absolute value of $x_?$"
. written: "\left| x_? \right|"
. description: "The absolute value $|x| = x$ if $x \ge 0$ and $-x$ if $x < 0$."
Id: "f75ee806-0ba7-4585-8183-d7f6355ed4cc"


[\real.supremum:of{S}]
Defines: M is \real
when: S \:(nonempty)::subset:/ \reals..R
expresses:
. forAll: x is \real
  where: x "in" S
  then: x \:real.leq?:/ M
. forAll: M' is \real
  where:
  . forAll: x is \real
    where: x "in" S
    then: x \:real.leq?:/ M'
  then: M \:real.leq?:/ M'
Documented:
. called: "supremum of $S?$"
. written: "\sup(S?)"
. description: "The least upper bound (supremum) $\sup(S)$ of a set of real
                numbers."
Id: "d9762902-b78e-43a8-981d-47ec829c9552"


[\real.infimum:of{S}]
Defines: m is \real
when: S \:(nonempty)::subset:/ \reals..R
expresses:
. forAll: x is \real
  where: x "in" S
  then: m \:real.leq?:/ x
. forAll: m' is \real
  where:
  . forAll: x is \real
    where: x "in" S
    then: m' \:real.leq?:/ x
  then: m' \:real.leq?:/ m
Documented:
. called: "infimum of $S?$"
. written: "\inf(S?)"
. description: "The greatest lower bound (infimum) $\inf(S)$ of a set of real
                numbers."
Id: "181bf9bc-8b82-4962-9a70-1f64dd384ea7"


SectionTitle: "The Completeness Axiom"
Id: "04cc8ce6-8bdd-49d3-8e76-52dd47ef4e73"


Text: "The hallmark of the real numbers is Dedekind completeness: every nonempty
       subset that is bounded above has a supremum."
Id: "bc931815-1d01-4658-817f-efe57c5b2cf3"


[\completeness.of.reals]
Theorem:
given: S \:(nonempty)::subset:/ \reals..R
where:
. exists: M is \real
  suchThat:
  . forAll: x is \real
    where: x "in" S
    then: x \:real.leq?:/ M
then:
. exists: sup is \real
  suchThat: sup = \real.supremum:of{S}
Documented:
. called: "Completeness of the Real Numbers"
. description: "Every nonempty set of real numbers bounded above has a least
                upper bound in $\mathbb{R}$."
Id: "b4fc64c6-378b-4e44-87c5-610045a90fe3"
